From 5be4fe4348f2e19a9239d12c0e8d52ab184c2012 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:13:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/28] esp32s3: RMT transmit channels

The RMT was an unimplemented region, so ESP-IDF's rmt_tx driver waited
forever for TX_END. Arduino-ESP32 3.x sends neopixelWrite() and
digitalWrite() on an RGB_BUILTIN LED (as on ESP32-S3 SuperMini and DevKitC
boards) through it, so such firmware stopped at its first LED write.

esp32s3.rmt keeps what is written to its registers and channel memory
(RMTMEM); TX_START sends a channel's symbols in virtual time (a tick is
an APB cycle times DIV_CNT), raising TX_THR_EVENT every TX_LIM symbols so
a driver can refill a ping-pong buffer, and TX_END at the end marker;
continuous mode repeats. Its interrupt goes to the matrix as
ETS_RMT_INTR_SOURCE. Pins are not driven; the bits sent (a long high is
a 1, as WS2812 LEDs read them) are kept as hex in the device's
last-frame property, with a frames count, for tests. Not modelled: the
receive channels, the carrier, loop counting, DMA.

esp32s3-rmt-test sends an LED's three bytes and reads them back, and
checks the threshold and end interrupts on a wrapping transmission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sb26stwPJiCMHhrBWZ2D9q
